/build*/
/compile_commands.json
/.cache/
*.user

# makepkg builds in place when run from packaging/aur, and everything it
# leaves behind is derived: the cloned source, the build tree, the staged
# package root and the package itself. One `git add -A` after a build
# otherwise stages ~90k lines of build output, plus the clone as an embedded
# repository. Note it also rewrites pkgver in the tracked PKGBUILD, which is
# a placeholder recomputed by pkgver() -- discard that rather than commit it.
/packaging/aur/src/
/packaging/aur/pkg/
/packaging/aur/plasma-lyrics-git/
/packaging/aur/*.pkg.tar.*
/packaging/aur/*.log
